anna: Heads-up: new user reported a SyntaxError from the Node quickstart in the README. They ran `node quickstart.js` on Node 16 and got 'Unexpected token' because our example uses top-level await.

anna: Current snippet in README (minimal):
```js
// quickstart.js
import Redwood from 'redwood';
const client = new Redwood();
const res = await client.generate({ input: 'hello' });
console.log(res.output);
```

anna: That example assumes Node 18+ or bundlers that support ESM and top-level await. New users on Node 14/16 or people copying into older projects hit a runtime error.

leo: Oof. We've seen this before. We should either change to an async IIFE or add a note about "requires Node 18+" and show an alternative.

tony: I hit this yesterday in a Codespaces onboarding session. People copy/paste and then DM support. Small change, big impact.

anna: Suggested fix 1 (async wrapper):
```js
import Redwood from 'redwood';
const client = new Redwood();
(async () => {
  const res = await client.generate({ input: 'hello' });
  console.log(res.output);
})();
```

anna: Suggested fix 2 (clear Node version + npm init step): add a note: "Requires Node 18+ (or run with --experimental-top-level-await in older Node)." and update package.json engines in the sample repo.

leo: Also our README import line `import Redwood from 'redwood'` is stale for the new SDK shape in 2.x where it's `import { RedwoodClient } from '@redwood/inference';` — we should check SDK parity across languages. The quickstart in docs and the samples repo are mismatched.

tony: Ack — looks like someone updated the SDK internals but not the docs. I'll open a tiny PR to sync both repos.

anna: Can we add a linter check for quickstart snippets? Something that runs the Node snippet on matrix: [node16, node18, node20] to ensure examples either work or explicitly state requirements.

ci-bot: Suggested job added to docs CI draft: docs/snippet-smoke -> matrix(node-version: [16,18,20]). Currently queued as a proposal.

docs-bot: Created ticket DOCS-501: "Node quickstart: remove top-level await, sync imports with SDK 2.x, and add node engine note". Linked PR: https://github.com/redwood-inference/docs/pull/325 (draft).

leo: Nice. When you open the PR, can you also update the samples/quickstart repo so both remain consistent? We should add a test in samples that runs the quickstart with node 18 in CI.

tony: I'll update the samples repo and add a smoke test. Will ping for reviews.

anna: Thanks — small docs fix but will reduce a lot of onboarding friction.

leo: Also maybe add a one-line troubleshooting FAQ: "If you see SyntaxError after running quickstart, check Node version and use async wrapper."

anna: Agreed. I'll add that to the README FAQ section in the PR. :thumbsup:
